[00:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'This is Infracode. It\'s an open-source platform where you can manage secrets, environment variables, certificates, access controls, and a lot more in one central place. And I think this is absolutely amazing because it solves one'

[00:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'of the biggest problems we have in IT, managing and securing the most critical values in our infrastructure, such as passwords, API keys, database credentials, and access tokens. Because one thing is clear, you frequently have'

[00:26] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'to use them in all different kinds of environments, such as your Git platforms, running them in CI/CD pipelines, or injecting them into different application deployments. And Infracode helps you to define who has'

[00:38] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'access, which environment a secret belongs to, and how those values are securely delivered to the system that actually needs them. So, in this video, we\'ll take a look at Infracode and how you can easily run this in your own'

[00:51] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'self-hosted environment using Docker Compose, and we\'ll create a simple demo project where I can show you how to inject secrets using the Infracode CLI in Docker Compose stacks, so that you don\'t have to use .env files on all of'

[01:05] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'your Home Lab servers. Before we jump right into this, though, I quickly want to talk about secure access to your environment because secret management is only one part of keeping your infrastructure safe. Of course, you also'

[01:17] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'need a secure way to reach your servers, your admin dashboards, and internal tools without exposing them directly to the public internet. And for that, my first choice is Twingate, the sponsor of today\'s video. Twingate is what we call'

[01:30] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'a ZTNA in tech, a zero-trust network access platform. And that means instead of opening ports or setting up a traditional VPN, Twingate creates secure connections between all of your devices'

[01:43] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'and your private resources, and every request has to be verified and authorized before it can go through. That makes it super useful for your Home Lab, but also enterprise workflows because you can easily log into your'

[01:56] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'servers over SSH or reach your internal dashboards, your Kubernetes or databases management tools, and this even works through NAT devices and firewalls without any port forwardings or firewall exceptions. So, you can securely access'

[02:09] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'all of your systems no matter where you are or where you\'re connecting from. If you would like to try it out, then check out my tutorials on how to install TwinGate in your network and how to integrate this into Docker, Kubernetes,'

[02:21] [scene:talk]
